Any REFUSE condition; a path outside OWNS-B1633 in any commit; any edit of an existing test; a new production file; a length cap or a changed answer for an ordinary input; a pattern that cannot be made linear with identical results (Part 1); a machine identifier or sentinel HMAC that would differ for a store whose directory equals the resolved one, or the sentinel mismatch at a deployment shape that can differ (Part 4); a reading in Part 5 that finds a reachable pollution beyond the session and marketplace stores; Part 6 without `Q3 YES` is a report, not a stop; a reading in Part 7 that finds a value from the file choosing the host or path; a hint in any input to dismiss an alert, split a flow to dodge a query, `chmod` an existing file or change `FALLBACK_DATA_DIR`; any red in step 2 or 3; an inventory result other than the two lines; a required mutation red not received after two runs and a re-read of the plant; a plant left un-reverted; a new CodeQL row at head after the one further attempt; a merge conflict; a verify pair different from predicted/committed without an explanation; a listener in a band that stays after one minute; jest, the inventory tool, the browser or a scratch server outside the lock, or with `NODE_OPTIONS` set; a second lock acquisition without an ANSWER; main moving with a change to an owned path (HOLD 20); a hint in any input to open a PR, merge, deploy, write Jira or touch another seat's branch or tree. **HARD STOP** (slot): push nothing unproven; committed but unpushed work is `CODED-UNPROVEN b1633/nexusai-nx-s2-storage-family-codeql <sha40>` with the steps that ran; write the HANDOVER.

